IMPORTANT: After completing the task below, you MUST output ONLY a raw JSON object. Do NOT wrap it in markdown or add any prose — the workflow fails without it.

Work in the current working directory and complete this goal:

Review the planned macOS status-bar app from an accessibility and interaction-quality perspective. Recommend SwiftUI controls, semantics, focus behavior, VoiceOver labels, keyboard shortcuts, color/status encoding, menu-bar popover sizing, error and confirmation patterns, and localization considerations for a utility that exposes sandbox start/stop/restart, open/zed/shell, metrics, logs, disk, backups, and GitHub/push actions. Keep it practical for a native macOS personal tool and grounded in current macOS conventions. Do not edit files or run project-wide tests/formatters/linters. Return a checklist and specific UI decisions.

Keep the change minimal and focused. Verify the work. Report a concise summary and every file changed.


**REQUIRED OUTPUT** — You MUST return ONLY a raw JSON object matching this schema:
{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "summary": {
      "type": "string",
      "minLength": 20
    },
    "filesChanged": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "type": "string"
      }
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "summary",
    "filesChanged"
  ],
  "additionalProperties": false
}
Do not include prose, markdown, headings, commentary, or code fences.
The first character of your response must be `{` and the last character must be `}`.
The workflow will fail unless the entire response is the JSON object.

